e bit too cheap but instead they  went with a sort of a fake faux leather  with stitching on the back I'm not sure  exactly if that makes it feel more  premium or if that still feels really  cheap this is one of those totally  subjective things that people are either  gonna love or hate I'm gonna have to  wait until I get my hands on it it comes  in a black a white or a pink look I'm  probably gonna pick up the black one and  ideally it will feel better than the  glossy plastic on the back of the galaxy  s4 but I'm just gonna have to wait till  I get my hands on it because I have no  idea how a phone with a leatherette back  is going to feel in my hand and of  course since this is the Galaxy Note 3  they made a lot of improvements to their  TouchWiz UI on top of Android 4.3 to  make it more useful for people who like  to use the stylus so they added a lot of  new features a lot more of them with a  stylus and of course they like to name  all these things so of course you have  action memos pen windows s finder  scrapbook I'm probably not going to use  any of these I ended up not using a lot  of the the stylus features with the  Galaxy Note 2 I did a galaxy note 2  revisited video  like six months after I was first using  it and it turned out I really stopped  using it as a stylist phone I just used  it as a regular big phone so I'm feeling  like it's gonna be the same way with the  note 3 but either way that's the way I  see it here with the galaxy note 3 again  I can't wait to get my hands on the  device the whole point is I haven't seen  the device yet I haven't held it yet I  don't know how the camera performs I  don't know how long the battery lasts I  don't know how well the device itself  performs as it as fast as the s4 is even  of course it's a Snapdragon 800 and it's  an incredible phone on paper but I can't  wait to get my hands on it and get you  guys the full review and all my  impressions like literally as soon as I  can  so stay stay tuned for that be 